Upstream pull request: none opened yet.

Ze can own the interface that carries the management request. A synchronous
power request must acknowledge and flush before service termination removes
that interface, then complete shutdown before scheduling the power operation.
The runtime helper states the requirement:
"A synchronous request MUST finish shutdown before scheduling powerFunc."

Testboot consumes reserved trailing whitespace and keeps one inactive-root
flag across retries. In-place FAT edits refuse growth beyond the existing
extent and add padding only before the final newline, preserving loader
metadata and adjacent file bytes.

The HTTP regression holds shutdown behind a barrier and observes acceptance
on an actual client connection before releasing it. Retained-extent tests
cover new and legacy command-line formats, loader headers, retries and an
exhausted extent with adjacent data.

Design: docs/architecture/appliance/ota-push.md and
docs/architecture/appliance/gokrazy-build-pins.md.

